{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121161","id":4028805584,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7wIrHQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121161","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121161.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121161.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121161","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121161/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121161/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121161/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/92cb8246a5b67b36482ea597f23773984f53cf37","number":121161,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Make it impossible to have more than one main thread, and don't release unnecessarily","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Should close https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121083, but not yet tested\r\n\r\nTwo problems:\r\n- There was previously no protection from multiple threads becoming the \"main thread\". If this had ever happened, hard to trace problems would ensue.\r\n- The main-thread-ness was previously dropped on all platforms, although only Android actually switches. This leads to unnecessary complications in other setup configurations.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nAwkward main-thread grabs now crash reliably instead of spuriously.\r\nThe main thread now stays main thread (in between `setup` and `setup2`) on all platforms that don't switch.\r\nMain-thread-ness is now released after teardown.\r\n\r\n#### Alternatives\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121083 could have been fixed in a variety of other ways:\r\n\r\n- `GDType` could stop checking for main-thread-ness. I'd really like to avoid this since we're still churning `GDType` pretty hard, and a predictable setup + teardown without multi threading complexity is critical. `GDType` might later drop this, but only in exchange for other safety guards:\r\n    - [PR #117443](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117443) could be used, but it would only tighten the vulnerable window, not erase it.\r\n    - `GDType` could use mutexes (only during setup) instead. This might be worth doing anyway, but it would add complexity I'd rather discuss than add now.\r\n- We could have tried to track down who creates the `GDType` between `setup` and `setup2`, but we've not quite established that this is illegal in the first place.\r\n\r\nPractically, I think the fix presented here is a useful safety improvement for the lifecycle anyway, making it more predictable, so that's why I opted for it.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_